## 🧠 Vector memory (optional — recommended for any project with real history)
{{ENABLE or "scaffolded but OFF until an OpenRouter key is provided"}}

- **Store:** ChromaDB at `{{./chroma/}}` (gitignored).
- **Embeddings / query model:** via OpenRouter (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, model `{{model}}`).
- **CLI:** `{{core}} memory add "<text>" [--tags …]` · `{{core}} memory query "<question>" [--k N]`.
- **Skill:** `{{memory-skill}}` — wraps the CLI so any role can record/recall without re-deriving the plumbing.
- **When to write:** `/finalize-session` records this session's durable facts/decisions.
- **When to read:** `/start-session` may run one `memory query` for the current task's context instead of loading the whole store.

> Why a vector DB over a flat file: the project's history outgrows what fits in context.
> Store everything; load only the few entries a given task needs. The always-loaded list
> above is the index; the vector store is the library.

## 🚫 What does NOT go here
Code structure, past bug fixes, git history, anything in CONSTITUTION.md or a playbook —
those are derivable or already documented. Memory holds only the non-obvious, non-derivable.
